SRC/hc_utils -- one change made for this collection===================================================compress.c (2026-09-15).  Six lines after #include <stdio.h>, inside#ifdef OSK, redefine putchar as fputc.  Microware's putchar macro evaluatesits argument twice when stdout is line-buffered -- a pipe or a terminal --so putchar(*bp++) when compressing and putchar(*--stackp) whenuncompressing skipped bytes there, and the output was corrupt.  Written toa file the macro evaluates it once, which is why it was always rightthere.  It still writes exactly those bytes: compressing SYS/termcap givesthe same 631 bytes, md5 c3694c4f0abc8ed599498e027b44945b, as before.CMDS/compress is this build, since 2026-09-18.  The period binary itreplaced wrote the same bytes to a file, and corrupted a pipe the same waythe unchanged source did.